    "UcFrontmatter": {
      "description": "Use-case frontmatter: `MarkdownFrontmatter` narrowed for the `uc` document type.\n\nParameters\n----------\ntype:\n    Fixed discriminator, always `\"uc\"`. Narrows the base's mandatory,\n    default-less `str` field to a `Literal[\"uc\"] = \"uc\"`, so a document\n    omitting `type` entirely still parses as a use case.\nstatus:\n    One of `\"draft\"`, `\"proposed\"`, `\"accepted\"`, `\"deprecated\"`,\n    `\"superseded\"`. Narrows the base's free-form `str = \"draft\"` default\n    to this closed five-value set, matching `uc/models/v1`'s own\n    vocabulary. Blank/absent still defaults to `\"draft\"` (inherited from\n    the base's `_default_blank_status_to_draft` validator, which runs\n    before this one).\n\nAll other fields (`id`, `created`, `updated`, `version`) are inherited\nunchanged from :class:`MarkdownFrontmatter`.",
      "properties": {
        "created": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Created"
        },
        "id": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Id"
        },
        "status": {
          "default": "draft",
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "uc",
          "default": "uc",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "updated": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Updated"
        },
        "version": {
          "default": "1.0.0",
          "title": "Version",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "UcFrontmatter",
      "type": "object"
    },
